invariant: INV-67
file: src/mldsa_vector.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mldsa-vector
reason: the AVX2 lanes' reduction adds no rounding bit, so it rounds
  down where mld_reduce32 rounds to the nearest multiple of 2^23. Every
  value stays congruent mod q, so a signature still verifies, but a
  coefficient whose bit 22 is set leaves the reduction q above the loops'
  value. bin/mldsa_vector_equiv_test compares coefficients exactly. Only
  an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds the binary for
  x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64, whose max model has AVX2.

--- old
    lanes t = _mm256_add_epi32(_mm256_srai_epi32(a, 23), bit22);
--- new
    lanes t = _mm256_add_epi32(_mm256_srai_epi32(a, 23), _mm256_andnot_si256(bit22, bit22));
